  "mechanismSummary": "Triethylamine removes the acidic S–H proton of thiophenol. The soft thiolate adds to the β-carbon of cyclohex-2-enone (conjugate, 1,4-addition), and the negative charge moves onto oxygen as an enolate. The triethylammonium ion protonates the enolate on carbon, giving 3-(phenylthio)cyclohexanone and regenerating triethylamine.",
